  ],
  "notes": "Describes an increase in speed or rate. Used both for physical acceleration (vehicles, objects) and for abstract processes gaining momentum (trends, reforms, decline).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {変化|へんか}が{加速|かそく}する: change accelerates\n- {成長|せいちょう}を{加速|かそく}させる: to accelerate growth\n- {少子化|しょうしか}が{加速|かそく}する: declining birthrate accelerates\n- {開発|かいはつ}を{加速|かそく}する: to accelerate development\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nUsed both intransitively ({車|くるま}が{加速|かそく}する, the car accelerates) and transitively with させる or を ({改革|かいかく}を{加速|かそく}する, to accelerate reform). The させる causative form is also common for transitive use: {成長|せいちょう}を{加速|かそく}させる.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {速|はや}める: to hasten — emphasizes making something happen sooner rather than increasing rate\n- {促進|そくしん}する: to promote/facilitate — focuses on actively pushing a process forward\n- {減速|げんそく}する: to decelerate — the opposite, slowing down",
